    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20-a3">

                <pb facs="0340" n="330" xml:id="pg330"/>

                <head>Appendix C to HD–15</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation<anchor n="11" xml:id="d20-f1"
                    />]</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Draft of Article 29 for Insertion in
                        the Peace Treaty With Bulgaria</hi></p>
                <p>The privileges and immunities of foreign subjects as well as the rights of
                    jurisdiction and of consular protection attaching to the Allied and Associated
                    Powers in Bulgaria in virtue of capitulations and usages as well as of treaties
                    can be made the subject of special conventions between each of the interested
                    Allied and Associated Powers and Bulgaria. Concerning these matters, the
                    principal Allied and Associated Powers will enjoy most-favored-nation treatment
                    in Bulgaria.</p>
                <p>The Allied and Associated Powers concerned undertake among themselves to
                    formulate only conditions to the stipulations of the present treaty. In case of
                    difference of opinion among them, the League of Nations will be called upon to
                    decide.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
